From: knulli <knulli@knulli>
Subject: [PATCH] treat the mali video driver as console, like kmsdrm

The mali-fbdev SDL2 backend is a console driver: one window, always the
size of fb0, and MALI_SetWindowSize() is a no-op.  Amiberry only knows
about KMSDRM, so it opens a resizable window instead, and every mode
change then calls SDL_SetWindowSize().  SDL updates window->w/h for a
non-fullscreen window even though the EGL surface keeps its original
size, so the GLES2 renderer computes its viewport against the wrong
output size and the frame lands off-screen -- a black display.

SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=software hides this because mali-fbdev has no
CreateWindowFramebuffer: SDL falls back to SDL_CreateWindowTexture,
whose internal renderer always stretches to the full output.

--- a/src/osdep/amiberry_gfx.cpp
+++ b/src/osdep/amiberry_gfx.cpp
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@
 	struct AmigaMonitor* mon = &AMonitors[0];
 	write_log("Getting Current Video Driver...\n");
 	sdl_video_driver = SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver();
-	if (sdl_video_driver != nullptr && strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "KMSDRM") == 0)
+	if (sdl_video_driver != nullptr && (strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "KMSDRM") == 0 || strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "mali") == 0))
 	{
 		kmsdrm_detected = true;
 		if (!mon->amiga_window && mon->gui_window)
--- a/src/osdep/gui/main_window.cpp
+++ b/src/osdep/gui/main_window.cpp
@@ -265,7 +265,7 @@
 	AmigaMonitor* mon = &AMonitors[0];
 	sdl_video_driver = SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver();
 
-	if (sdl_video_driver != nullptr && strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "KMSDRM") == 0)
+	if (sdl_video_driver != nullptr && (strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "KMSDRM") == 0 || strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "mali") == 0))
 	{
 		kmsdrm_detected = true;
 		if (!mon->gui_window && mon->amiga_window)
--- a/src/osdep/gui/ShowMessage.cpp
+++ b/src/osdep/gui/ShowMessage.cpp
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
 {
 	AmigaMonitor* mon = &AMonitors[0];
 	sdl_video_driver = SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver();
-	if (sdl_video_driver != nullptr && strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "KMSDRM") == 0)
+	if (sdl_video_driver != nullptr && (strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "KMSDRM") == 0 || strcmpi(sdl_video_driver, "mali") == 0))
 		kmsdrm_detected = true;
 	SDL_GetCurrentDisplayMode(0, &sdl_mode);
 
